of proton-proton collision data at $\sqrt{s}=13$ TeV recorded by the ATLAS
detector in 2015 and 2016. The search is performed for the Higgs boson decaying
to two photons in association with a $Z$ boson decaying to two leptons. The
data are found to be consistent with the expectation from the background-only
hypothesis. Exclusion limits are set on the production cross-section of the
$HH\to\gamma\gamma ZZ\to\gamma\gamma\ell\ell$ process in different intervals of the
diphoton invariant mass. The observed (expected) upper limit on the production
cross-section is found to be 2.44 (2.44)$\pm$0.82 (0.77) fb at 95% confidence
level for a Higgs boson mass of 125.09 GeV.
